      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_1",
          "text": "Amos 5 overturns confidence in a favorable \u201cday of the LORD.\u201d The chapter joins that reversal to concrete accusations against people who sell the righteous, exploit the poor, corrupt the gate, and seize what others have pledged. Its rejection of festivals, offerings, songs, and music is directed at worship joined to exploitation, not at ritual or music as such.",
