      "title": "Prophetic and political setting",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "The chapter uses courtroom, treaty, and royal imagery familiar in the ancient world, but the prophet speaks for the LORD. Royal \u201cday\u201d imagery helps explain the metaphor while Amos presents the LORD as judge and deliverer. The northern kingdom also lived under pressure from larger empires, so political instability and imperial danger form part of the chapter\u2019s setting.",
