      "title": "Israel under pressure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_3",
          "text": "After the united monarchy divided, the northern kingdom was centered on Samaria. Amos speaks into real national crises rather than an abstract religious setting. The warnings address covenant breach and imperial pressure, while the later siege and fall of Samaria belong to the contested transition from Shalmaneser V to Sargon II, usually placed around 725\u2013720 BCE. The precise sequence of capture, conquest, deportation, and provincial rule should remain qualified.",
