    {
      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "title": "Justice, worship, and textual difficulty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_4",
          "text": "\u201cLet justice roll down like waters\u201d is a communal demand grounded in the gate, debt, land, labor, and worship concerns named across the chapter. It should not be reduced to one modern party, nation, ideology, or church program. The day of the LORD is darkness for those who presume upon it, not a timetable for later speculation. Amos 5:25\u201327 also has a complicated textual and reception history: Acts 7 quotes a Greek form, while Sikkuth and Kiyyun remain difficult designations that should not be confidently equated with later names.",
